1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
A sound soul dwells within a sound mind, and a sound body.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:33,000
I have come to strike a bargain.

3
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:52,000
I'm falling down to my shadow.

4
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
I'm falling down to my shadow.

5
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
I'm falling down to my shadow.

6
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:12,000
I'm falling down to my eyes.

7
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:16,000
See you in your dreams, yeah, baby.

8
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Out of my baby.

9
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Oh no.

10
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Oh no.

11
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,000
I'm falling down.

12
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Black, red, brown, brown

13
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:38,500
信じてくれたなら

14
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:43,000
When you lost it were young

15
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Forever with your soul

16
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
見上がれば輝く

17
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,000
月のように

18
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:22,000
メデューザ

19
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
She's here

20
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Even with her soul protect on I can tell

21
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
That's her behind this door

22
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Medusa

23
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
There's someone there

24
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
I'm so thirsty

25
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Maybe I could have a glass of water

26
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Witch

27
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Medusa

28
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,000
There's a little girl at the door

29
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Is there something I can do for you?

30
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
You did this

31
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
I don't understand what you mean

32
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Whatever did I do?

33
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
It's because of you that Crona's suffering so much

34
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Oh my, so Crona's a friend of yours?

35
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Tell me, how's he doing?

36
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,000
How do you think he's doing?

37
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
You was like this by his own mother

38
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Oh, I've been very worried about him

39
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
He's always been such a fragile child, you see

40
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
How could you do this to him?

41
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
You call yourself a parent?

42
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Do you think I could see Crona?

43
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:26,000
A mother shouldn't be separated from her child for so long

44
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Would you drop the act?

45
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Of course I'm not sure how he'll react

46
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Seeing me in such a sad state like this

47
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:35,000
I told you, drop the act!

48
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Calm down, Maka, breathe

49
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Let's get out of here

50
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,000
It's useless anyway

51
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Talking to someone like her won't get you anywhere

52
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Do you hear me, Medusa?

53
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:50,000
You're gonna spend the rest of your life in that dark little cell

54
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Enjoy, it's more than you deserve

55
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Come on

56
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Come on

57
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Sorry, children, but I'm afraid it's not going to end like this

58
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
Don't you agree?

59
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Professor Stein

60
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
The cards are cut

61
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Medusa surrenders to the DWMA?

62
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Yeah, now that was a bit of a shock, huh?

63
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,000
We were all convinced that Medusa was dead

64
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:37,000
And then she waltzes up to the Academy and surrenders?

65
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
It's my fault

66
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:45,000
I was certain that Stein and I had finished her off for good in that battle

67
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Don't forget, we're dealing with a witch here

68
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
With them, anything's possible

69
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
And that's just the beginning

70
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Medusa's no ordinary witch

71
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:00,000
We can't handle her using ordinary means

72
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Why did you come here?

73
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,000
To see you, of course

74
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:11,000
Did you think they'd let you walk out of here whenever you want?

75
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
The world has begun to move, Stein

76
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
You feel it, I know you do

77
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Besides, you know I'd never bet on something I wasn't guaranteed to win

78
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:24,000
We'll see, won't we?

79
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Are you feeling all right, Stein?

80
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Your voice is trembling a bit

81
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:34,000
I can hardly bear this, watching as the madness slowly consumes you

82
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Don't you have other things to worry about right now?

83
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,000
How could I not be worried?

84
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
I need you

85
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Are you ready to join me?

86
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
You aren't telling the whole truth

87
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,000
You must have had another motive besides talking to me

88
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:52,000
You have to learn to free yourself from the rules

89
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Otherwise you'll never be saved

90
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Come over to my side

91
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Together we'll make things happen

92
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,000
We'll see the dawn of a new world

93
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,000
It's time, Stein

94
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
You know that, don't you?

95
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,000
Terribly sorry

96
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Am I interrupting?

97
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Get out of here, Stein

98
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:18,000
You know you shouldn't leave your lab right now

99
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
You're coming with me

100
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,000
Let's go

101
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Now where are you taking me?

102
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Let me guess, to an interrogation room?

103
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Well, am I right?

104
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Please, mister

105
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Why am I all tied up like this?

106
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,000
My arms hurt and I can barely breathe

107
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Give it up

108
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
I'm not falling for it

109
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
Oh?

110
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
You talked to me though, didn't you?

111
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
So I won that round

112
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Pretty soon you're gonna be the one doing the talking

113
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,000
Now then

114
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Shall we get started?

115
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Torture's a bad idea

116
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Oh, you can do it, of course

117
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
But you should think carefully before hurting my body

118
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Or didn't you realize that this body was borrowed?

119
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Damn her

120
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,000
She's thought of everything, hasn't she?

121
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:33,000
As a parent you should show some sympathy

122
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
That child deserves her body back

123
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:39,000
I only need it until my magic fully recovers

124
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,000
It's alone

125
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
I'll give it back sometime

126
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Just when we thought you couldn't sink lower

127
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
You might want to be more careful in how you speak to me

128
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
You don't even know what I've come here to offer

129
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
I could be the saving grace you need

130
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,000
Oh, yeah?

131
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:57,000
I have certain information that could prove useful to the Academy

132
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,000
Information?

133
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
Take me to the Reaper and we'll talk, otherwise you get nothing

134
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,000
Don't be ridiculous

135
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,000
You're in no position to make demands

136
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Anyway, you aren't exactly trustworthy

137
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Why should we believe anything you have to say?

138
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
I was afraid it would come to this

139
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:20,000
If that's your attitude, I suppose I'll just have to make you believe

140
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:32,000
I was good with a shovel back when I was alive, too

141
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:34,000
I was that kind of man

142
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,000
I don't mind all the digging

143
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
But what could Medusa be hiding here?

144
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
This looks like...

145
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,000
Brew

146
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
We ran all the tests

147
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
This is the real Brew

148
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:13,000
She gave it to you in order to convince you to let her speak with me directly?

149
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:15,000
She's insisting on it

150
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Apparently she wants to make a deal with us

151
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
A deal, huh?

152
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:23,000
I've got no damn clue what that witch has up her sleeve

153
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Why is she willing to give up Brew to us this easily?

154
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
And how did she get her hands on it?

155
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,000
There's a lot about this we don't understand

156
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,000
I don't know what she's up to

157
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
But one thing we can count on

158
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
She wants to use us somehow

159
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,000
I'm sure of that

160
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:42,000
At any rate, she's right

161
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
I do think I should speak with her in person

162
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Are you sure?

163
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Yes

164
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,000
I want you to bring her here immediately

165
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,000
So?

166
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Grim Reaper

167
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,000
Yeah, yeah

168
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,000
You're enjoying yourself immensely, aren't you?

169
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Because of you, the world is now on the brink of total disaster

170
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
That may be true

171
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,000
But I'd still like to show you my gratitude for speaking with me

172
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,000
Hmm

173
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Let's get to the point

174
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
First there's the matter of these restraints

175
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Perhaps you could remove them

176
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,000
They are quite uncomfortable

177
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,000
And surely with you standing right there, they aren't really necessary

178
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Don't play with me

179
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:27,000
If you wanted those restraints off, you could have removed them yourself a long time ago

180
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
But it would be meaningless if I took them off myself

181
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,000
Hmm

182
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,000
Hmm

183
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Ugh

184
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Don't try anything

185
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:39,000
I won't think twice about ripping you apart

186
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,000
REAPER CHOP

187
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:49,000
Um, your death, sir?

188
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Oh, come on

189
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
After all she's done, she deserves at least one chop

190
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,000
Okay

191
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,000
The Reaper chop

192
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:59,000
That's the thing I hated most about the academy

193
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Even when I was the school nurse, I lived in fear of that chop

194
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,000
It's awful

195
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Come here

196
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,000
Now

197
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
What deal were you talking about?

198
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:10,000
My bloomers are showing

199
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,000
Huh?

200
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
He's treating me like a child

201
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,000
I miscalculated

202
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Excuse me, Reaper

203
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:18,000
Could you put me down?

204
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Bloomers! Adorable!

205
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:24,000
My mucca wore those when she was little

206
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
So sweet little baby bloomers

207
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
This is getting too weird

208
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
I need to get them to focus somehow

209
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:36,000
Now if we could return to the topic we were discussing

210
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Here's a question

211
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
What do you think bloomers would look like on a grown woman?

212
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,000
It's been done

213
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Centuries ago

214
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:44,000
They used to wear them all the time

215
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Ugh

216
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,000
But if they did it now

217
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,000
Wouldn't it be a bit creepy?

218
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:50,000
A philosophical discussion on women's underwear

219
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
That's enough!

220
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Stop it right now!

221
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Oh

222
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,000
We shouldn't talk about this in front of a lady

223
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:59,000
That's not what I was concerned about!

224
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Right

225
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:02,000
Now about this deal of yours

226
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,000
No, put me down right now!

227
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,000
I don't promise again!

228
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:09,000
If you don't stop that, I'm going to kill you

229
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,000
What's her problem?

230
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Can't she even take a little joke?

231
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
And it was expertly executed too

232
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,000
Repetition is the foundation of humor

233
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Three times as best

234
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Absolutely, I agree

235
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,000
However, since we were interrupted

236
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:22,000
We'll have to start from the beginning now

237
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:25,000
Hey, where do you think you're going?

238
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,000
Oh, come back!

239
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,000
I won't pick you up by the hood anymore

240
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Is that a promise?

241
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
What do you say, Reaper?

242
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
The conditions of the deal are fair

243
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:39,000
If anything, I think you're getting the better end of the bargain

244
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:43,000
What I'm offering is the answer to the question weighing heaviest on your mind right now

245
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:47,000
We won't agree to a thing until we hear your conditions

246
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Fine, if you don't want to tell us, I'll pick you up by the hood again

247
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Hey, you promised!

248
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Sweet adorable bloomers!

249
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,000
Quit that already, it's creepy

250
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:05,000
Just put me down, I'll explain the deal, but let me go

251
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,000
You honestly call yourselves adults?

252
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,000
As for what I have to offer

253
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,000
Will the Kishin's location do?

254
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Hmm, you're lying

255
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,000
We put all our effort into finding him

256
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
And we haven't uncovered a single trace

257
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Death Scythe has a point there

258
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,000
How can we be sure you aren't lying?

259
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
Can you prove what you say is true?

260
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,000
No, I can't

261
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:33,000
At least not while I still don't have your complete trust

262
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:35,000
Is that so?

263
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,000
Alright then, give us the location

264
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
We'll check and see if it's true

265
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
You can't really think I'd be stupid enough to do that

266
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Why not?

267
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:46,000
If I tell, what's your incentive to keep your end of the deal?

268
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
What is our end of the deal?

269
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
It's not that complicated, really

270
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:54,000
I want to be released from Academy custody immediately

271
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:57,000
I'll also expect you to guarantee my safety, of course

272
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,000
That's all you want?

273
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:01,000
Yes, that's all of it

274
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Hmm

275
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Unfortunately, I don't believe that's a condition we can accept

276
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,000
That's too bad

277
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:12,000
I suppose this means you'd rather live under the thumb of arachnophobia

278
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,000
